WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
I discovered that something that was
unimaginable just a few years ago

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.000
is happening now.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.140
Chinese and American scientists collaborating to secure nuclear materials--

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.220
uranium --from the far corners of the globe.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.340
I'm Rich Stone

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.160
I'm the international news editor at
Science Magazine.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.780
My story for the Pulitzer Center

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.300
is about Chinese and American scientists working together

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.720
to save the world

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.340
This is really part of my beat at Science

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.720
I have a rather unusual beat

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.540
it's weapons of mass destruction

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.960
and particularly difficult countries to report from

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.340
such as Iran and North Korea

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.620
Even though I lived in China for 5 years

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.640
I never got permission to go to China's

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.280
nuclear weapons design laboratories.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.460
It's a real object of frustration for me

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.100
I thought well how can i nibble at the
edges of the story?

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.240
20 years ago there was a report in the US Congress

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.040
about Chinese spying in the nuclear complex

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.440
it was allegations of spying that China
vehemently denied

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:11.520
but because of that report

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.480
American scientists had been
barred

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.640
from the Chinese Academy of Engineering physics.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.300
There's been no collaboration practically speaking for the past 20 years.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.740
So the fact that they're getting together now is pretty significant.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.320
So for the story I reported from Beijing

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.920
and from Accra, Ghana.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.720
I visited a new center for excellence in nuclear security

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.980
that the US and the Chinese
worked together to establish

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.440
pretty amazing complex

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:43.000
they have a bunker where nuclear materials

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.900
--special nuclear materials--are stored

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.820
I got to go inside the bunker with the scientists there.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:54.420
The first thing you notice going in: the
razor wire-- curlicues of razor wire--

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.260
hanging from the ceiling.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.220
The scientists pointed to a yellow line just

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.700
a few inches from from my feet and 
said if you step past that line

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.320
the razor wire falls down on you.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.380
He was joking.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.700
It wouldn't fall down on you but

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:16.340
what happens with the razor wire is it's lowered to the floor when staff are not there

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.360
at an operating nuclear facility storing nuclear materials like this

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:25.640
it's one measure to slow any potential nuclear smugglers.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.820
So ever since 9/11 the US government has been very concerned

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.900
about securing loose nukes, first of all nuclear weapons

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.300
and also any nuclear materials in countries

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.580
that are not one of the nuclear weapon states.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.160
And there's a lot of this nuclear
material out there.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.100
So the US has worked throughout Eastern Europe

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.500
to move out highly enriched uranium.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:55.120
There are smaller amounts that are also scattered
around the globe

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:00.400
including at research reactors that China produced

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.600
in the 1980s and 1990s and shipped to

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.900
5 countries.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.060
It's a very unusual kind of research reactor

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:18.540
These reactors are in Ghana, Nigeria, Iran,

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.600
Pakistan, and Syria.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.060
It's not really necessary at this point

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.480
to have that kind of weapons-usable nuclear fuel

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.480
The reason that is not necessary now is

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.250
that Chinese and American scientists
worked together for 10 years on a project

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:40.200
to redesign the reactor core of the
miniature neutron source reactor to

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:45.390
convert it to run on low enriched
uranium which cannot be used for a

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.989
nuclear weapon unless it's further
enriched and that's not easy to do and

00:03:48.989 --> 00:03:53.740
so Ghana was the first reactor outside
China to be converted.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.520
I was in Ghana

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.380
when the new core was brought in and
installed into the reactor.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.800
The highly enriched uranium core had already been taken out.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.000
But when I visited it had not

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.720
left the country yet.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.980
One of the nuclear regulators from Ghana remarked

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:16.080
when we passed by it--somewhat
mysteriously--he said there's a little

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.400
God under there
that's like what do you mean and he

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:25.220
whispered to me that's it that's the old
core so it was not something that they

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.640
wanted to have lying around.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.440
Finally last month in August the plane

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:35.570
took the uranium back to China. Now the
Chinese and Americans are going to work

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:39.890
together in the next conversion which is
going to be in Nigeria, this coming

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:44.780
spring. People hope that this will lead
to more cooperation

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.980
among the nuclear weapons scientists.

